        A("\n**Requirement text that changes:** PA-3 'reads the AWG output through a sense divider, that divider's ratio (PA-4) and every ladder tap (PA-9)' stays, the part becoming the ADS1220 with 4 inputs. PA-4 'One switch moves the divider's bottom end from the mid-rail reference to the reference (the ladder's top tap, PA-8), and the precision ADC reads the result' -> 'One switch moves the divider's far end between the reference and ground, with the AWG held at a positive level, so the ratio comes from two readings of the tap'. PA-8 'The ladder's top tap is the buffered reference itself' -> 'is the reference output itself'. PA-9 'built from eight discrete 249 Ω 0.1% resistors ... (3 in parallel at the bottom, 5 in series above) ... about 330 Ω worst and 2.3 mA from the reference buffer' -> 'nine 680 Ω 1% resistors (C23228), 680/3 at the bottom and three pairs above: 3 inner taps and the top, 312 Ω worst and 2.4 mA from the reference, re-read at every calibration'. D11 'up to 8 taps on A2 to A9, eight 249 Ω 0.1% resistors' -> '3 taps and the top, on four of A2 to A9'.\n")
